  "question": {
    "text": "The first orbital of H is represented by<br />\r<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></math> , where <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is Bohr's radius. The probability of finding the electron at a distance r, from the nucleus in the region dV is",
