  "solution": {
    "text": "This can be obtained by the solution of Schrodinger wave equation as follows<br />Probability <math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ψ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br />As orbital is spherically symmetrical<br />So <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />i.e., <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Hence, probability <math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ψ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>.",
